Subject: [PATCH 02702/11362] [outer-loop] Build from upstream llama.cpp
 RELEASE tag b9714 (MTP is in master/release) -- not the diffusion PR

Operator was right: MTP (--spec-type draft-mtp) is in UPSTREAM master/release now -- speculative.h maps
{'draft-mtp', COMMON_SPECULATIVE_TYPE_DRAFT_MTP} + arg.cpp has the --spec-type CLI + download_mtp
auto-detect. (My earlier 'not on master' was a shallow-fetch artifact; the value is behind the symbol, not
the literal string.) Switched the build kernel from PR 24423 (diffusion branch) to a clean reproducible
RELEASE TAG b9714 -- smaller, no diffusion-example baggage, the release the operator referenced. Self-verify
MTP-symbol assert retained. Pushed v4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 scripts/kaggle/build_verify_llamacpp_mtp.py | 10 ++++++----
 scripts/kaggle/kernel/main.py               | 10 ++++++----
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

